---

Vendored from https://github.com/dashersw/liquid-glass-js rather than
installed as an npm dependency: the library ships only as plain <script>
globals, not a package, so there is nothing for `npm install` to manage.
container.js and button.js live alongside this LICENSE (loaded at
runtime as real <script> tags, see ../../lib/loadLiquidGlass.ts); its
glass.css lives at ../../app/liquid-glass.css instead, as a normal
bundled import, since a stylesheet has none of the load-order
constraints the scripts do. See frontend/README.md and DOCEXP.md's
Slice entry on this integration for why.
